# Form Submission Methods: Email + WhatsApp Simultaneously

When a user submits the "Contact" or "Inquire Now" form on your website, you can send the inquiry to **both your Email address and your WhatsApp number** at the exact same time.

To ensure a smooth user experience, we send the email silently in the background so the user only sees the WhatsApp application opening up for them.

Here are the two best methods to achieve this:

---

## Method 1: Using a Free Third-Party Service (Web3Forms)
This method is perfect if you are hosting your website on a platform that **does not support backend code** (like Vercel, Netlify, GitHub Pages, or basic static hosting). 

Web3Forms gives you an API key to send emails directly from your JavaScript code.

### 1. Get an Access Key
1. Go to [Web3Forms](https://web3forms.com/).
2. Submit your email (`angelevent2211@gmail.com`) to get a free Access Key.

### 2. Update your HTML/JavaScript
Update the `submit` event listener in your [index.html](file:///d:/JavaScript/angel-event-planning/index.html) and [contact.html](file:///d:/JavaScript/angel-event-planning/contact.html) to first hit the Web3Forms API, and then open WhatsApp.

```javascript
document.getElementById('whatsappFormHome').addEventListener('submit', async function (e) {
  e.preventDefault();
  
  const name = document.getElementById('home_name').value.trim();
  const message = document.getElementById('home_message').value.trim();
  const submitButton = this.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');

  if (!name || !message) return;

  // Temporarily disable the button
  submitButton.innerText = "Sending...";
  submitButton.disabled = true;

  try {
    // 1. Send Email silently in the background
    await fetch("https://api.web3forms.com/submit", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: {
        "Content-Type": "application/json",
        Accept: "application/json",
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        access_key: "YOUR_WEB3FORMS_ACCESS_KEY_HERE", // Replace with your actual key
        subject: `New Inquiry from ${name}`,
        name: name,
        message: message,
      }),
    });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Email failed to send", error);
  }

  // Restore the button
  submitButton.innerText = "Send via WhatsApp";
  submitButton.disabled = false;

  // 2. Open WhatsApp
  const phoneNumber = "917722811133";
  const whatsappMessage = `Hello Angel Event Solution!%0A%0A` +
    `Name: ${encodeURIComponent(name)}%0A` +
    `Message: ${encodeURIComponent(message)}%0A%0A` +
    `Looking forward to your reply.`;

  const whatsappURL = `https://wa.me/${phoneNumber}?text=${whatsappMessage}`;
  window.open(whatsappURL, '_blank');
});
```

---

## Method 2: Using PHP (Recommended for cPanel / Shared Hosting)
This is the most professional method. If your website is hosted on GoDaddy, Hostinger, HostGator, or any standard cPanel web host, you likely have PHP and standard mail servers available. 

This method requires creating a small backend PHP script.

### 1. Create `send_mail.php`
Create this file in your root folder (next to [index.html](file:///d:/JavaScript/angel-event-planning/index.html)). It acts as a secure middleman to fire off the email.

```php
<?php
// send_mail.php

if ($_SERVER["REQUEST_METHOD"] == "POST") {
    // Read the incoming JSON payload from Javascript
    $data = json_decode(file_get_contents("php://input"), true);
    
    $name = htmlspecialchars(trim($data["name"]));
    $message = htmlspecialchars(trim($data["message"]));
    
    if (empty($name) || empty($message)) {
        http_response_code(400);
        echo json_encode(["status" => "error", "message" => "Fields cannot be empty."]);
        exit;
    }
    
    // Set up email details
    $to = "angelevent2211@gmail.com"; 
    $subject = "New Inquiry from " . $name;
    $email_body = "Name: $name\n\nMessage:\n$message";
    
    // Email Headers
    $headers = "From: noreply@yourdomain.com\r\n" .
               "Reply-To: noreply@yourdomain.com\r\n" .
               "X-Mailer: PHP/" . phpversion();
               
    // Send the Email
    if (mail($to, $subject, $email_body, $headers)) {
        http_response_code(200);
        echo json_encode(["status" => "success"]);
    } else {
        http_response_code(500);
        echo json_encode(["status" => "error", "message" => "Failed to send email."]);
    }
} else {
    http_response_code(405);
    echo json_encode(["status" => "error", "message" => "Method not allowed"]);
}
?>
```

### 2. Update your HTML/JavaScript
Just like Method 1, change the `submit` event listener to fetch our new `send_mail.php` file internally before moving on to WhatsApp.

```javascript
document.getElementById('whatsappFormHome').addEventListener('submit', async function (e) {
  e.preventDefault();
  
  const name = document.getElementById('home_name').value.trim();
  const message = document.getElementById('home_message').value.trim();
  const submitButton = this.querySelector('button[type="submit"]');

  if (!name || !message) return;

  // Temporarily disable the button
  submitButton.innerText = "Processing...";
  submitButton.disabled = true;

  try {
    // 1. Send the data to your own PHP script securely
    await fetch('send_mail.php', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: {
        'Content-Type': 'application/json',
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({ name: name, message: message })
    });
  } catch (error) {
    console.error("Error sending email:", error);
  }

  // Restore the button
  submitButton.innerText = "Send via WhatsApp";
  submitButton.disabled = false;

  // 2. Open WhatsApp
  const phoneNumber = "917722811133";
  const whatsappMessage = `Hello Angel Event Solution!%0A%0A` +
    `Name: ${encodeURIComponent(name)}%0A` +
    `Message: ${encodeURIComponent(message)}%0A%0A` +
    `Looking forward to your reply.`;

  const whatsappURL = `https://wa.me/${phoneNumber}?text=${whatsappMessage}`;
  window.open(whatsappURL, '_blank');
});
```

---
> **Tip:** Regardless of the method you choose, you will need to update the Javascript snippet in **both** [index.html](file:///d:/JavaScript/angel-event-planning/index.html) (for `#whatsappFormHome`) and [contact.html](file:///d:/JavaScript/angel-event-planning/contact.html) (for `#whatsappForm`).
